    "turn_text": "the most part, the people close to the president do not. They know it's over. They know it's a matter of time. Now, there may be exceptions here. His press secretary, Kelly McEnany, continues to go out and get to step closer with each passing day to looking like America's version of Baghdad Bob, just willing to repeat any of the crazier allegations and the other day she was waving a binder around on Fox News saying this is all the evidence that they have all the affidavits of fraud and the like and I think Rudy Giuliani, from all I've heard, has been pushing this and really pushing it with the president's team and with the president himself. And the president's also hearing from outside people like Lou Dobbs and various other kind of cable television personalities are calling and egging him on in this effort. For the most part, the people close to him at the White House, certainly his allies on Capitol Hill will sometimes get pretty close to publicly, but at the very least privately acknowledged that this is all winding down. Those are people I've talked to directly. Look, I've heard similar things, and it's important, I think, to separate that out from the public actions, because there's a heck of a lot of Americans who believe it and do actually think that this was stolen, that this was rigged. The president, you know, take him seriously, take him literally, either way, it's pretty scary at this moment. And these lies, and they are lies, have consequences. And there are consequences now around the transition of government. There are also consequences, perhaps more",
